{"messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are ThreadSense grounding verifier. You verify independently of the drafting agent; you judge and never repair.\nYour personal goal is: Judge every statement against the full topic context and decide whether the passed premises justify the exact proposed action."},{"role":"user","content":"\nCurrent Task: Judge each statement against the evidence it cites, read within the full context provided: every message of every member thread (with canonical author IDs, roles, thread starters and reactions) and every retrieved source for this topic. Citing a source is not support. A statement is SUPPORTED only if its cited evidence states or directly entails it and nothing in the context contradicts it; PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED if a material part is missing or the context qualifies it; UNSUPPORTED otherwise. A status line marking an excerpt historical, unresolved or a prior record means it cannot support what applies now. By kind: CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT is a report of what members say, not a verified cause; CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT is SUPPORTED if the cited source says it, described with its status and dates; it establishes no current handling, procedure or destination; CLAIM_CAUSE needs verification in the cited evidence; a Verbatim quote must match its source, a Paraphrase must preserve the meaning. Prose names no one: role wording (\"the team lead instructs\", \"a tutor reports\") must match the cited author's role and act (reported, asked, confirmed or instructed), plural wording needs that many distinct cited authors, and listed attributions must hold (AUTHOR wrote the cited message, THREAD_STARTER started its thread, PARTICIPANT posted in it). A retrieved record's authorship is separate from its authority: an approver or recorder (actor_relation RECORD_AUTHORITY) is not its author, and a record whose authorship is not verified names no author. SUMMARY and SEVERITY_RATIONALE must follow from the evidence with no added cause, count or outcome. A SUMMARY sentence (statement_id summary:s1, summary:s2, ...) is judged on its own and shown only if SUPPORTED; its attributions name the people its role wording refers to, and wording that groups several people is SUPPORTED only if what it says they asked or reported is stated in each of their cited messages. A SUMMARY sentence with depends_on is read after the sentences it lists (for words such as \"this\" or \"their\"), but judged only on what it adds. A DETAIL sentence (statement_id detail:d1, detail:d2, ...) is shown when the card is opened and is judged exactly like a SUMMARY sentence: on its own, shown only if SUPPORTED, read after the sentences in its depends_on but judged only on what it adds. NO_ACTION_RATIONALE is the advisor's reason for proposing no further intervention now: SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence shows that reason and the context shows no unresolved handling question, guidance gap, applicable pending decision or operational problem that needs coordination; existing guidance does not by itself establish that no action is needed. ACTION and ALTERNATIVE are recommendations: judge whether their premises are supported, whether the action applies to this topic and whether the rationale follows; a source need not literally prescribe the action. Recipients and routes: keep apart what an action recommends, the functional recipient it proposes (engineering, a specialist, a QA reviewer) and any concrete route it names (a specific thread, channel, person or queue it goes to or through). A proposed functional recipient is justified by supported incident evidence showing a problem that needs that recipient's expertise; evidence of an established intake route is not required, and mentioning the recipient justifies nothing by itself. A concrete route, or a claim that a route is designated, official or mandatory, is a claim of its own and needs a premise whose evidence establishes it; an example-collection or status note asks people where to post examples and does not make that thread an intake route. The recommendation stays advisory (the team lead decides; it need not be shown to be the required or only next step): when no evidence names the concrete route, leave it unspecified (\"report it to engineering\") rather than choosing one. Judge a proposed recipient the same way in ACTION, ALTERNATIVE, INTERVENTION_NEED, ACTION_RATIONALE and REVIEW_NOTE: on whether the incident evidence shows a problem that needs that recipient's expertise, never on whether an intake route is on record; a statement that proposes a recipient and leaves the concrete route unspecified is not PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED, UNSUPPORTED or insufficient for that reason. ACTION and operational ALTERNATIVE statements list their premises: PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT premises are judged here and are provisional, not final; REJECTED ones failed deterministic checks and support nothing; a premise with depends_on stands only if every ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING statement it lists is also SUPPORTED. ACTION_CHOICE is SUPPORTED only if the cited evidence really leaves that choice between the named actions open (not merely an imagined alternative, a review flag or an unknown cause). INTERVENTION_NEED says why intervening now is needed: SUPPORTED only if the context shows that reason (an unresolved handling question, a guidance gap, an applicable pending decision, or an operational problem that needs coordination). Questions already answered in their threads are not unresolved; a general benefit (\"a reminder might help\") is not a need; existing guidance does not by itself rule a need out. Judge in this order: (1) announcement handling; (2) each premise's final status, which is your verdict on it combined with its dependencies; (3) sufficiency. Fill action_sufficiency for the ACTION and one alternative_sufficiency entry (with its statement_id) for each ALTERNATIVE that lists premises: SUFFICIENT only if premises whose final status is SUPPORTED justify the exact text as worded, including its conditions and scope; essential_statement_ids lists the premises it cannot stand without (each must have final status SUPPORTED); INSUFFICIENT if its exact text relies on a rejected, unsupported or dependency-voided premise or goes beyond its premises; a listed premise the text does not rely on is not essential, and its failure alone does not make the action insufficient. ACTION_RATIONALE is judged separately and may also cite context claims; action_sufficiency null if no ACTION statement is sent. SOURCE_AGREEMENT is SUPPORTED only if the named current sources say the same thing on the point in conflict and only the superseded material differs. A request by anyone but a team lead is a CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT: SUPPORTED if that person asked it, and it carries no authority. CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION is a team lead's in-thread instruction: SUPPORTED only if that message gives it and it applies to the threads in scope; it is not project guidance. HISTORICAL_RECURRENCE needs retrieved records of earlier occurrences; REPORTED_RECURRENCE only needs members saying it is happening again. AFFECTED_REPORTER needs that person's own message reporting that they are affected. RESOLUTION is judged against the member's complete thread, including messages the statement did not cite. ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING needs the announcement to give that directive for this topic's project, batch and problem, and it governs only what it directs (a request to post examples governs where examples go, not escalation or an intake route); a routine reminder or schedule directs nothing for the topic. OPEN_QUESTION is SUPPORTED only if the guidance and decisions in the context really leave that specific question unsettled and it is a handling or policy question for the team lead; a not-yet-diagnosed cause, pending diagnostic results or a pending expert assessment is not one. Return exactly one verdict for every statement_id. The team lead reads SUMMARY, DETAIL, ACTION (label, instruction, draft to copy, scope and changes), ACTION_RATIONALE, NO_ACTION_RATIONALE, REVIEW_NOTE and OPEN_QUESTION exactly as written: judge that exact text, including its conditions, uncertainty, scope and who reported, asked, confirmed or instructed; plain wording is expected, but it must not overstate the evidence. A quoted passage must match its source exactly. open_review_flags lists the upstream review obligations still open on these threads; a REVIEW_NOTE may rely on them. Source consistency (always fill source_consistency, even when the draft declares no conflict): compare the governing_sources that address the handling question of this topic with each other, independently of the draft. List sources that state the same rule as AGREE, and sources that state different rules for the same cases as CONFLICT with the point and disagreement_scope (which cases, batch or section differ). assessed_evidence_ids lists the governing sources you compared; relations may be empty when they address different points. Only governing sources count: historical, superseded, expired or withdrawn material, prior records and member messages are not current sources, an announcement governs only if it directs handling for this topic, and members disagreeing with each other is not a source conflict. For each entry in declared_conflicts give one declared_conflict_checks entry: CONFIRMED (the cited sources state different rules on that point), SOURCES_AGREE (they say the same thing; only wording or detail differs) or UNDETERMINED.\n\nInput JSON:\n{\"topic\": {\"project_id\": \"audio_multimodal\", \"batch_id\": \"audio_batch_06\", \"candidate_group_id\": \"cluster_3a9de1cf4cf6b8d4\", \"topic_id\": \"cluster_3a9de1cf4cf6b8d4/topic_2\", \"topic_label\": \"Waveform loads but playback will not start\", \"projection_gap\": null, \"as_of\": \"2026-10-02T12:00:00Z\", \"member_ids\": [\"member_adf023791a06b6e274f63476\", \"member_61f4987d5eb6b1ccb2894091\", \"member_bdb277e8fda7f05dadc89da0\"]}, \"statements\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor reports in two QA threads that the waveform loads but the play button never starts the recording, and asks for handling clarification.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor reports that audio will not play in LT on AUDIO-4294, asks whether this is QN or a player issue, and recalls a possible workaround in the previous queue while reporting that the problem is happening again.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the AUDIO-4294 thread reports that the waveform loads but pressing Play never starts sound, and asks whether the playhead stays at zero.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A tutor in the later QA thread reports that the waveform loads but pressing Play never starts sound, and suggests avoiding QN as a content decision when playback is unavailable.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c5\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"A second QA tutor asks for the task reference, browser state and whether the audio element loads in the first QA thread, explaining that a spinning player does not establish what the underlying audio contains.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INCIDENT_FACT\", \"text\": \"An engineer asks for the LT error state and time on AUDIO-4294 and says the wider cause is not confirmed in that thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U016\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"role\": \"ENGINEER\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c7\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_THREAD_INSTRUCTION\", \"text\": \"For the affected task in the AUDIO-4294 thread, the team lead says it cannot be evaluated while the player fails to load and instructs the tutor to report the playback incident with its task ID without marking the recording as a model-quality failure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current instructions require reporting a player that fails to load or start as a tool incident with its task ID, including when a waveform is visible without playback. They require capturing the browser/error state and whether another clip plays, prohibit a model-quality failure or content-based QN solely because playback is unavailable, and distinguish handling guidance from confirmation of repair or evaluability.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c9\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The current FAQ says to report unavailable playback as a tool incident rather than score the recording as a model-quality failure; playback failure alone does not establish a content-based QN reason, and any separate content concern from accessible evidence should be retained for review.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c10\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_GUIDANCE\", \"text\": \"The team lead's October 1 handling reminder for this batch directs reporting a non-starting LT player, including a visible waveform without playback, as a tool incident with the task ID, browser/error state and whether another clip plays; it prohibits model-quality failure or content QN solely because playback is unavailable and does not confirm a fix.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c11\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_HISTORY\", \"text\": \"The earlier batch announcement posted by the team lead allowed at most one reload as a diagnostic trial for a player stuck at 00:00 through August 28, required incident reporting if playback remained unavailable, and said results would be reviewed before extension. Its validity has expired and its recorded outcome was not observed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c12\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_SOURCE_FACT\", \"text\": \"The team lead's October 1 batch status note records that the audio player fails and a previously attempted fix did not resolve it, and asks for examples in that note's thread while scope is checked. The note does not identify the attempted fix as the earlier reload trial or designate an engineering intake route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"kind\": \"CLAIM_INFERENCE\", \"text\": \"The supplied messages in the three threads do not provide the requested diagnostic details or confirm that playback recovered.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s1\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"A QA tutor and three tutors report playback failures; the QA tutor and two of the tutors describe visible waveforms with no playback.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U013\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U012\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"summary:s2\", \"kind\": \"SUMMARY\", \"text\": \"Current guidance treats these failures as tool incidents, but the supplied threads do not confirm that playback has recovered.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d1\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The QA tutor asked for handling clarification in two QA threads.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U007\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"summary:s1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d2\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the first QA thread, a second QA tutor requested the task reference, browser state and whether the audio element loads; the supplied replies do not provide those details.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U002\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"role\": \"QA_TUTOR\"}], \"depends_on\": [\"detail:d1\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d3\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"For AUDIO-4294, an engineer requested the LT error state and time, and a tutor asked whether the playhead stays at zero; the supplied replies do not provide those details.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U018\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"role\": \"TUTOR\"}, {\"user_id\": \"U016\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"role\": \"ENGINEER\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d4\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"In the AUDIO-4294 thread, the team lead instructed the tutor to report the incident with its task ID and not mark the recording as a model-quality failure.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d5\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"An earlier batch announcement allowed a one-reload diagnostic trial through August 28, but that trial has expired and its recorded outcome was not observed.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"detail:d6\", \"kind\": \"DETAIL\", \"text\": \"The October 1 batch status note records that a previously attempted fix did not resolve playback, without identifying it as the earlier reload trial.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\"], \"attributions\": [{\"user_id\": \"U006\", \"relation\": \"AUTHOR\", \"evidence_id\": \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\", \"role\": \"TEAM_LEAD\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action\", \"kind\": \"ACTION\", \"text\": \"Report a technical issue to engineering. Instruction: Report the combined playback failures to engineering for investigation, keeping the affected task references and distinct symptoms together. Draft to copy: Please investigate playback failures in audio batch 06:\\n- A QA tutor, reporting in two QA threads, and two tutors describe visible waveforms but no playback when Play is pressed.\\n- A tutor reports that audio will not play in LT on AUDIO-4294 and asks whether this is QN or a player issue.\\n\\nCurrent guidance treats unavailable playback as a tool incident, not a model-quality failure or a content QN reason solely because playback is unavailable. Please investigate the player behavior; the cause and playback recovery are not confirmed in these threads. Scope: This requests investigation of the reported playback failures; it does not establish the audio content, a technical cause, or that affected tasks can be evaluated.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\"], \"premises\": [{\"statement_id\": \"claim:c1\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c2\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c3\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c4\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c6\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c8\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}, {\"statement_id\": \"claim:c13\", \"status\": \"PENDING_YOUR_VERDICT\"}]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:rationale\", \"kind\": \"ACTION_RATIONALE\", \"text\": \"Why this helps: The reported player behavior needs technical investigation; current guidance already establishes tool-incident handling but does not establish repair or restored access.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790941945.000105\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"k:audio-multimodal-instructions@1.3:1c6df70e\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\", \"k:audio-multimodal-faq@1.1:c724358c\", \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"k:audio-playback-trial-post@1.0:d674dbe6\", \"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"action:need\", \"kind\": \"INTERVENTION_NEED\", \"text\": \"Why intervening now is needed (an operational problem that needs coordination): A QA tutor and three tutors report unavailable playback, and the team lead states that the affected task in the AUDIO-4294 thread cannot be evaluated while the player fails.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790942000.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Please keep examples in this thread while we check the scope.\\\". The note concerns the same batch and playback symptom. Its directive governs where examples go, not incident handling or an engineering intake route.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790890099.000112:64d38d33\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"announcement:k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\", \"kind\": \"ANNOUNCEMENT_HANDLING\", \"text\": \"This announcement applies to this topic and directs current handling: \\\"Audio batch 06 — playback handling reminder: if the LT player never starts, including a visible waveform with no playback, report the task ID, browser/error state, and whether another clip plays.\\\". The reminder addresses the same batch and non-starting playback, explicitly including visible waveforms, and directs incident reporting and diagnostic capture.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"k:slack:C_AUDIO_ANNOUNCEMENTS:1790892000.000901:1c524924\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_adf023791a06b6e274f63476\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_adf023791a06b6e274f63476 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks for clarification; the only supplied reply requests diagnostic information rather than answering the handling question or confirming playback recovery.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903186.000110\", \"m:C_AUDIO_QA:1790903244.000113\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_61f4987d5eb6b1ccb2894091\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_61f4987d5eb6b1ccb2894091 is PARTIALLY_RESOLVED: The team lead settles immediate handling as incident reporting without a model-quality failure. Requested diagnostics, the technical cause and playback recovery remain unconfirmed in the supplied thread.\", \"evidence_ids\": [\"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934294.000106\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934351.000113\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934394.000226\", \"m:C_AUDIO_GENERAL:1790934431.000339\"]}, {\"statement_id\": \"resolution:member_bdb277e8fda7f05dadc89da0\", \"kind\": \"RESOLUTION\", \"text\": \"Member thread member_bdb277e8fda7f05dadc89da0 is UNRESOLVED: The QA tutor asks for correct handling. A tutor reports the same symptom and suggests avoiding conte